            <fr:meta name="toc">true</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <fr:p>Homotopy Type Theory (HoTT) is a type theory whose types can be interpreted (usefully) as topological spaces, complete with loop spaces, homology, and homotopy groups. <fr:link type="external" href="http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/">The HoTT book</fr:link> is the best introduction that I know of. Also Egbert Rijke's <fr:link type="external" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082">Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory</fr:link>.</fr:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
